  "decision": "Equal dimension budgets prevent indicator-count dominance; the poverty/HDI pair shares one deprivation allocation. Alternative weights and single-indicator substitutions change scores and fine ordering, so no precise league-table interpretation is warranted. Weights remain explicit project trade-offs, not externally approved importance coefficients.",
  "limitations": [
    "27-region descriptive sensitivity, not sampling uncertainty or causal validation.",
    "Comparisons use two-decimal released scores and average tied ranks; ties are not arbitrarily broken.",
    "Fixed min-max reference and additive aggregation remain modeling assumptions; this analysis does not claim full methodological robustness.",
    "Leave-one-indicator-out scenarios are declared diagnostics, never a missing-data production rule."
